HSE human failure procedures and shift handover (@engineering-source-human-factors: 0, is #reference) { r_005E57B92B1E14D9A4710D1943
Health and Safety Executive, English web guidance: [Managing human failures](https://www.hse.gov.uk/humanfactors/topics/humanfail.htm), [Procedures](https://www.hse.gov.uk/humanfactors/topics/procedures.htm), and [Shift handover](https://www.hse.gov.uk/humanfactors/topics/shift-handover.htm).

**Actual inspection — 1 November 2026:** human-failure definitions, selected error/violation discussion, management principles and common pitfalls; procedure rationale and design principles; handover purpose, preparation/exchange/cross-checking, communication and incoming-information needs. The displayed procedure page date is 12 January 2026; the handover page shows 29 October 2024. These are retrieved web pages, not a claim to have inspected all of HSG48, the linked research reports or current requirements for every jurisdiction.

Read those sections in that order. The common paper-board investigation applies the arguments to original simulated cases. It supplies no HSE experiment, human-error probability, industrial operating procedure or certification.

